{"id": 26, "ts": 1780634086.2750494, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I agree with James and Emily that Candidate\u202fC remains the strongest overall fit. The evidence we have\u2014100\u202f% reliability, a proven ability to keep calm in a crisis, quick correct decision\u2011making, and a consistently positive crew atmosphere\u2014covers the core safety\u2011critical criteria of operational reliability, stress resilience, decision quality, and crew cooperation. While C\u2019s difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric attitude, and limited willingness for further education are noted, they have not manifested as safety\u2011critical behavior and are outweighed by the concrete strengths we\u2019ve observed. In contrast, Candidate\u202fA still lacks any documented evidence of reliability or crew\u2011cooperation, and Candidate\u202fD\u2019s moody, loner traits raise unanswered concerns about teamwork. Candidate\u202fB\u2019s uncooperative and grumpy behavior, plus the weak numeric memory, remain significant red flags. Given the current evidence, I would continue to recommend Candidate\u202fC."}
